SUMMARY:(2444) Lederle hides a mag 14.5 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(2444) Lederle hides a magnitude 14.5 star\, seen from Rasapūd
 ipalem\, IN.\nThe predicted edge passes 3 km to the NNW\, so a miss is lik
 ely — but a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of
  all.\nClosest approach 23:34:31 IST\, give or take 5 s. The star is 13° 
 up in the WSW · dark sky.\nIt fades 2.8 magnitudes for up to 4.3 s on the
  centre line\, and the path is 30 km wide\, give or take 18 km.\nFinder ch
 art\, the map and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026
 -09#2026-09-13-2444-lederle-717440
